# Sequence Platform frontend - environment configuration (example).
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables reach
# the browser bundle, and everything in that bundle is public: never put a
# secret, token, or key in a frontend environment variable.
#
# Origin of the deployed backend API, with no trailing slash and no `/api`
# suffix (the application appends `/api` itself).
#
# Leave empty for local development: every request stays relative and the Vite
# dev server proxies /api to http://127.0.0.1:8000 (see vite.config.ts). A
# production build must set it to the deployed backend's origin, and that
# backend must list this site's origin in its CORS_ORIGINS setting, e.g.:
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://sequence-platform-api.onrender.com
VITE_API_URL=
